### ============================================================
### Real Estate Management System — REST API Tests
### Compatible with: VS Code REST Client extension
###                  JetBrains HTTP Client
###
### Setup:
###   1. Start the backend:  cd backend && npm run dev
###   2. Run database.sql to seed the default admin user
###   3. Execute "Login as Admin" first — copy the returned
###      accessToken and paste it in @adminToken below
###   4. Execute requests top-to-bottom in dependency order
### ============================================================

@baseUrl    = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@adminToken = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@empToken   = PASTE_EMPLOYEE_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### SECTION 0 — Health & Status
### ============================================================

### 0.1 Health check (no auth)
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 0.2 API status
GET {{baseUrl}}/status
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### SECTION 1 — AUTH
### ============================================================

### 1.1 Register (first admin bootstrap)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name":     "System Administrator",
  "email":    "admin@company.local",
  "password": "Admin@1234",
  "role":     "admin",
  "phone":    "+966 50 000 0001"
}

###

### 1.2 Login as Admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email":    "admin@company.local",
  "password": "Admin@1234"
}

###

### 1.3 Get current user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 1.4 Refresh access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

###

### 1.5 Change own password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "current_password": "Admin@1234",
  "new_password":     "Admin@5678"
}

###

### 1.6 Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================================================
### SECTION 2 — USERS  (Admin only)
### ============================================================

### 2.1 List all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 2.2 List users — filter by role
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=employee&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 2.3 Create an employee
# @name createEmployee
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name":     "Sara Al-Rashid",
  "email":    "sara@company.local",
  "password": "Employee@1234",
  "role":     "employee",
  "phone":    "+966 50 000 0002"
}

###

### 2.4 Get user by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 2.5 Update user
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name":  "Sara Mohammed Al-Rashid",
  "phone": "+966 50 000 0099"
}

###

### 2.6 Admin reset password
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/2/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "password": "NewPass@9999"
}

###

### 2.7 Deactivate user
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/2/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 2.8 Activate user
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/2/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 2.9 Delete user
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================================================
### SECTION 3 — PROPERTIES
### ============================================================

### 3.1 Get property types (lookup dropdown)
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/types
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.2 List properties — default page
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.3 List properties — with filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties?status=available&listing_type=sale&min_price=100000&max_price=1000000&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.4 Search properties
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties?search=villa&sort=price&order=ASC
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.5 Create a property
# @name createProperty
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "type_id":        1,
  "type":           "Apartment",
  "title":          "Modern 3BR Apartment in Riyadh",
  "description":    "Spacious and fully furnished apartment in the heart of Riyadh with premium finishes.",
  "location":       "Riyadh",
  "address":        "12 King Fahd Road, Al Olaya District, Riyadh",
  "area":           185.5,
  "rooms":          5,
  "bedrooms":       3,
  "bathrooms":      2,
  "floor":          7,
  "price":          750000,
  "payment_method": "cash",
  "owner_name":     "Khalid Al-Otaibi",
  "owner_phone":    "+966 55 123 4567",
  "listing_type":   "sale",
  "status":         "available",
  "is_featured":    true
}

###

### 3.6 Get single property (ID from 3.5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.7 Update a property
PUT {{baseUrl}}/properties/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "price":       720000,
  "description": "Updated: price reduced. Spacious apartment with panoramic city view."
}

###

### 3.8 Change property status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "status": "reserved"
}

###

### 3.9 Get property images
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/1/images
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.10 Upload property images (multipart)
# NOTE: change the file paths to valid files on your machine
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties/1/images
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="photo1.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-assets/photo1.jpg
------boundary--

###

### 3.11 Delete a property image
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/properties/1/images/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 3.12 Delete a property
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/properties/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================================================
### SECTION 4 — CUSTOMERS
### ============================================================

### 4.1 Get CRM pipeline counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 4.2 List all customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 4.3 List customers — filter by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?status=new&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 4.4 Search customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?search=Ahmed&sort=created_at&order=DESC
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 4.5 Create a customer
# @name createCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name":          "Ahmed Al-Mansour",
  "phone":         "+966 50 987 6543",
  "email":         "ahmed.mansour@example.com",
  "property_type": "Apartment",
  "location":      "Riyadh",
  "budget":        800000,
  "budget_min":    500000,
  "notes":         "Looking for a 3-bedroom apartment in North Riyadh. Prefers new buildings.",
  "status":        "new",
  "source":        "walk-in"
}

###

### 4.6 Get single customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 4.7 Update a customer
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customers/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "budget":  900000,
  "notes":   "Updated budget. Also interested in villas.",
  "location": "Riyadh, North"
}

###

### 4.8 Change customer pipeline status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/customers/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "status": "interested"
}

###

### 4.9 Assign customer to employee (admin only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/customers/1/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "employee_id": 2
}

###

### 4.10 Employee lists own customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{empToken}}

###

### 4.11 Delete a customer
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================================================
### SECTION 5 — REPORTS
### ============================================================

### 5.1 Dashboard KPI stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.2 Properties report (all time)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.3 Properties report — date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/properties?from_date=2026-01-01&to_date=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.4 Properties report — single agent
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/properties?agent_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.5 Customers report
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.6 Customers report — filter by employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/customers?employee_id=2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.7 Financials report (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/financials
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.8 Financials report — date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/financials?from_date=2026-01-01&to_date=2026-06-30
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.9 Agent performance report (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.10 Agent performance — date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/agents?from_date=2026-01-01&to_date=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================================================
### SECTION 6 — ERROR CASES (should return errors, not 500s)
### ============================================================

### 6.1 Login with wrong password  → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email":    "admin@company.local",
  "password": "WrongPassword1"
}

###

### 6.2 Access protected route without token  → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

###

### 6.3 Employee tries to access user management  → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{empToken}}

###

### 6.4 Create property — missing required field  → 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "title": "Incomplete Property"
}

###

### 6.5 Get non-existent property  → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 6.6 Register with duplicate email  → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name":     "Duplicate Admin",
  "email":    "admin@company.local",
  "password": "Admin@1234",
  "role":     "admin"
}

###

### 6.7 Create customer — missing required phone  → 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "No Phone Customer"
}
